# TF2's stock Grenade Launcher's drum (`procedural_chamber`,
# specs/tf2/weapons_more.md 9.6): how it turns per shot and per grenade
# loaded, in the Demoman's own view. Two shots 0.8 s apart with
# `cl_autoreload 0`, then `+reload` loads both; every frame at 60 fps
# (`host_framerate 0.016667`; `wait 2` is one frame here) as `gld_NNN`.
# The turn is read from the pictures (the chambers against the frame's
# top strap and rivet); the arms' sequences leave weapon_bone_2 on
# weapon_bone_1 (VScript, the server's view model, every tick), so all
# of the drum's turning is the client's own.
#   tools/tf2ref/tf2ref.py scene tools/tf2ref/scenes/gl_drum.tf2 --out <dir>
mp_disable_respawn_times 1
tf_weapon_criticals 0
host_framerate 0
bot_kick all
player red demoman
sleep 3
use tf_weapon_grenadelauncher
cl_drawhud 0
r_drawvgui 0
cl_autoreload 0
setang 0 90 0
sleep 3
host_framerate 0.016667
wait 4
movie gld
wait 20
+attack
wait 2
-attack
wait 96
+attack
wait 2
-attack
wait 96
+reload
wait 2
-reload
wait 300
endmovie
host_framerate 0
cl_autoreload 1
